    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d309-a1">

                <pb facs="0684" n="564" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg564"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Board of License Commissioners for
                        Ontario</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Federal Prohibition Commissioner</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Haynes</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Toronto</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-07-04"><hi rendition="#italic">July 4,
                        1922</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir</hi>: I yesterday received your telegram
                    which reads as follows: “Word received today that the Secretary of State has
                    conveyed desired request through British Embassy. Confidential.”</p>
                <p>Unfortunately, the Session of Parliament had closed several days previously, so
                    that it will be impossible to obtain the desired legislation this year. I am
                    disappointed about this, for the proposed legislation would greatly assist in
                    preventing the smuggling of liquors into your country.</p>
                <p>Yours very truly,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">James Hales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
